      "stdout": "Evidence collected.\n\n**Repo Python range** (`pyproject.toml`): `requires-python = \">=3.11,<3.14\"` — capped below 3.14 because pydantic-core has no cp314 wheel yet; 3.11 floor.\n\n**Python support lifecycle** (`devguide.python.org/versions` + PEP 602): 3.11 (security-only, EOL Oct 2027); 3.12 (security-only, EOL Oct 2028); 3.13 (bugfix, EOL Oct 2029); 3.14 prerelease (Oct 2025, EOL 2030).\n\n**Comparison:** The declared range aligns well with upstream — 3.11–3.13 are all actively supported; 3.14 is excluded intentionally (rust-transitive build failure). The only gap is that 3.11 hits EOL in Oct 2027 (security-only now); maintaining `>=3.11` is acceptable short-term but should be raised to `>=3.12` by that point.\n\n**Recommendation (with citations):**\n- Keep `<3.14` cap until pydantic-core ships cp314 wheels (per `pyproject.toml` comment).\n- Keep `>=3.11` for now; plan to bump floor to `>=3.12` before Oct 2027 (3.11 EOL).\n- Consider testing against 3.13 (current bugfix branch, best-supported) as primary CI target.\nSources: repo `pyproject.toml`; https://devguide.python.org/versions/; https://peps.python.org/pep-0602/ (saved in memory).\n",
